<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsushima Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsushima is a mountainous island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> Strait between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and the Korean peninsula, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a> Prefecture. Its rulers, the Sō clan, depended on trade with Korea and managed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s relations with the Joseon court, including the trading post at Busan. The island was raided by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1274 and attacked by Korea in 1419, and the Japanese navy destroyed the Russian fleet in the strait nearby in 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsushima-island.jpg" alt="Tsushima Island" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Image Science and Analysis Laboratory, NASA-Johnson Space Center. &quot;The Gateway to Astronaut Photography of Earth. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsushima_Island_ISS034.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
